>> title: Irish Stew
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: lamb, potatoes, irish, one-pot, stew
>> counters: Diner, One Pot
>> aka: lamb stew, Irish lamb stew
>> pairs-with: no-knead-bread
>> servings: 6
>> time: 3 hr
>> slack: forgiving — lamb shoulder at an hour and a half is only softer at two, and the stew is better the next day; the potatoes are the part with the window, going in for the last forty minutes because from the start they thicken the pot into a mash instead of sitting in it
>> step.3: simmer covered 1 1/2 hr
>> step.4: simmer 40 min more

Brown @lamb shoulder{3%lb}(1.4 kg; cut in 2-in pieces), @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @vegetable oil{2%Tbs} in a heavy #pot{}.

Layer @yellow onions{2%large}(sliced), @carrots{3%large}(cut in 2-in lengths), @pearl barley{1/4%cup}(50 g) over @&(~1)browned lamb{}.

Simmer @&(~1)pot{} with @lamb stock{4%cup}(950 mL; or water), @thyme{4%sprigs}, @bay leaf{1} for ~{90%min}.

Add @floury potatoes{2%lb}(900 g; Russets, quartered) to @&(~1)stew{} for ~{40%min}.

Finish @&(~1)stew{} with @flat-leaf parsley{2%Tbs}(chopped), @black pepper{1%tsp}.
